diff --git a/docs/notes.md b/docs/notes.md
index 4badf9f..bb9f95e 100644
--- a/docs/notes.md
+++ b/docs/notes.md
@@ -62,3 +62,15 @@
   - Players with `0` points never win; if fewer than `N` players have `> 0` points, all of them win.
   - `"Reset winners"` (`POST /moderate/games/:id/reset_winners`): clears all winners.
   - `GameBroadcaster` pushes rendered HTML payloads over ActionCable (`game_moderator_#{game.id}` and `game_play_#{game.code}`) so both big screen and player phones update instantaneously.
+
+## Release 5: Question Timer
+- **Quiz Settings**:
+  - `Quiz#timer_minutes` and `Quiz#timer_seconds`: integer columns, `null: false`, default `0`, validated `>= 0`.
+  - Exposed as `"Timer minutes"` and `"Timer seconds"` number fields in quiz settings (`app/views/moderate/quizzes/_form.html.erb`).
+  - `0` minutes and `0` seconds (`quiz.timer_duration_seconds == 0`) means no timer (`quiz.timer_enabled? == false`).
+  - Excluded from the JSON export format (`Quiz#as_export_json`).
+- **Live Game Countdown & Auto-Finish**:
+  - While a question is open (`game.question_open?`) and `quiz.timer_enabled?`, the moderator's big screen renders `<div class="stage-timer" id="question-timer" data-timer-remaining-ms="...">M:SS</div>` (e.g., `"1:30"` or `"0:05"`).
+  - Players never see the timer.
+  - Remaining time is computed from `game.question_opened_at + game.timer_duration_seconds.seconds - Time.current`, so reloading the page continues the countdown from where it is rather than restarting it.
+  - At `0:00`, the question finishes automatically (`Game#finish_question_if_expired!` via `Concurrent::ScheduledTask`, state polling, and controller checks) as if the moderator clicked `"Finish"`, broadcasting the closed-question state to both moderator and players. The moderator can still click `"Finish"` earlier.
